Remove MOUNT_SPEC from the sandbox.

MOUNT_SPEC is HOST[:CTR_TARGET]. CTR_TARGET defaults to the host path —
the same default `sbx mount` applies — so `sbx umount SANDBOX HOST` undoes
`sbx mount SANDBOX HOST`. A mount created with an explicit CTR_TARGET
must pass the same target back here to umount its bind.

HOST may be absolute or relative; relative paths are resolved against the
current working directory before submission, and ./.. segments are cleaned —
so HOST resolves the same way it did at mount time as long as cwd matches.
The host path need not still exist on disk: the allowlist is the source of
truth, so a path that was deleted after mounting can still be revoked.

For a stopped sandbox, removes the saved mount so it will not be restored
on the next start. The sandbox does not need to be started first.

If CTR_TARGET is neither mounted nor saved, the command fails without
revoking access to HOST. Pass the target used when mounting. A successful
unmount revokes access through every mount of the same HOST. Other mounts
remain in place but lose access to that host path.

Usage:
  sbx umount SANDBOX MOUNT_SPEC [flags]

Examples:
  # Revoke the default mount (bound at the host path)
  sbx umount my-sandbox /Users/me/extra-data

  # Revoke and umount the bind at /workspace/data
  sbx umount my-sandbox /Users/me/extra-data:/workspace/data

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for umount

Global Flags:
      --cloud   Dispatch to Docker Cloud Sandboxes API instead of local sandboxd (supported by a growing set of verbs — run 'sbx --cloud --help' for the current list)
  -D, --debug   Enable debug logging
